title: Rival Organisations
subtitle: Alliance, attack, concession or individual recruitment—never another party's leadership.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_rival_organisations_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_rival_organisations_timer = 2
card-image: img/poland/cards/coalition-council.webp

= Rival organisations persist between crises

PiS currents, allied or former United Right parties, KO component parties and
their successors retain membership, cohesion, organisation and their own
decisions. Lewica may influence one relationship this month. It cannot choose
a rival leader or transfer a caucus wholesale.

- @alliance
- @attack
- @concession
- @recruit

@alliance
title: Build an alliance with the most compatible autonomous organisation
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Relation and cohesion rise; Lewica autonomy narrows.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A permanent liaison team requires one resource.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
const candidates = (Q.rival_group_records || []).filter(function(record) {
    return record.active &&
        (record.kind == "party" || record.kind == "association") &&
        !["po", "ko_party", "pis_apparatus"].includes(record.id);
}).sort(function(first, second) {
    return second.relation - first.relation;
});
const target = candidates[0];
if (target) {
    target.relation = Math.min(100, target.relation + 7);
    target.cohesion = Math.min(100, target.cohesion + 2);
    Q.news_headline = "Lewica builds an alliance channel with " + target.name;
} else {
    Q.news_headline = "No autonomous rival organisation accepts an alliance channel";
}
Q.party_unity -= 1;
!}

A permanent liaison team means somebody in the building is now paid to keep
another organisation's leadership content. The channel is real, and it narrows
what Lewica can say without making a telephone call first.

- #poland_card_finish

@attack
title: Publicly attack the strongest hostile rival current
subtitle: No resource cost. The target hardens while Lewica gains definition.
on-arrival: {!
const candidates = (Q.rival_group_records || []).filter(function(record) {
    return record.active && record.relation < 25;
}).sort(function(first, second) {
    return second.organisation - first.organisation;
});
const target = candidates[0];
if (target) {
    target.relation = Math.max(-100, target.relation - 6);
    target.cohesion = Math.min(100, target.cohesion + 3);
    Q.news_headline = "Lewica publicly attacks " + target.name;
} else {
    Q.news_headline = "Lewica attacks the rival apparatus without personalising its leadership";
}
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
!}

The attack lands on an apparatus rather than a face, which is more accurate and
much less satisfying. The target closes ranks, and the difference between the
two parties becomes legible to people who previously could not name one.

- #poland_card_finish

@concession
title: Offer a social-policy concession to the welfare-conservative channel
subtitle: Negotiated opposition concession: household-policy pressure +2, not implementation; rights-oriented caucuses dislike it.
on-arrival: {!
const target = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "pis_welfare";
});
if (target) {
    target.relation = Math.min(100, target.relation + 6);
    target.cohesion = Math.min(100, target.cohesion + 1);
}
Q.pis_relation += 3;
Q.government_favors += 1;
Q.household_policy_pressure += 2;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession";
Q.last_policy_authority = "Party-to-party parliamentary channel";
Q.last_policy_implementation = "Pending a competent cabinet and enacted measure";
Q.news_headline = "A social concession opens a vote without giving Lewica control of PiS";
!}

Household policy gains a vote and the rights caucuses gain a grievance. It is a
parliamentary concession, not a programme: PiS keeps its own leadership, its
own timetable, and the credit if the measure is ever implemented.

- #poland_card_finish

@recruit
title: Recruit one individual from the least cohesive autonomous organisation
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. One person moves; the organisation survives.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Individual vetting and local integration require one resource.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
const candidates = (Q.rival_group_records || []).filter(function(record) {
    return record.active &&
        (record.kind == "party" || record.kind == "association") &&
        record.mp_count > 1;
}).sort(function(first, second) {
    return first.cohesion - second.cohesion;
});
const target = candidates[0];
if (target) {
    target.mp_count = Math.max(0, target.mp_count - 1);
    target.organisation = Math.max(0, target.organisation - 1);
    target.relation = Math.max(-100, target.relation - 3);
    Q.rival_individual_recruits += 1;
    Q.news_headline = "One vetted organiser leaves " + target.name + " for Lewica";
} else {
    Q.news_headline = "No individual recruitment clears the vetting process";
}
Q.local_network += 1;
!}

One organiser with a county behind them is worth more than a declaration signed
by a leadership. The organisation they left is weaker by exactly one person and
no more willing to talk to us than it was yesterday.

- #poland_card_finish
